"Connects one desired product outcome to researched customer opportunities, alternative solutions and the assumption tests used to evaluate them.\n\nUse when: Keep continuous discovery focused on an outcome. Compare multiple solutions for a selected customer need.\n\nAvoid when: Opportunities would be invented from feature requests without customer research.\n\nVisual grammar: A root outcome leads to opportunities and subopportunities. Candidate solutions branch beneath relevant opportunities. Assumption tests attach to solutions and remain distinct from delivery tasks.\n\nBuild: Define a measurable outcome and synthesize customer stories. Structure the opportunity space and select a focused target. Generate alternatives, identify assumptions and plan tests across promising solutions.\n\nCheck: Opportunities describe unmet needs rather than preferred features. Solutions remain hypotheses until supported by evidence. Every branch relates plausibly to the selected outcome.\n\nPitfalls: Attaching a favored solution before understanding the opportunity. Turning the tree into a commitment to build every branch.\n\nExample: A membership team targets renewal retention, investigates confusing renewal choices and tests several ways to improve understanding.\n\nAlternatives: Assumption map, Impact map."
